    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup leans heavily into the favorable matchup against Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez, who is anchoring a cluster of high-value starts for **Luis Arraez** (60.94), **Matt Chapman** (58.96), and **Jung Hoo Lee** (53.78). **Luis Arraez** earns the top spot in our rankings today; despite the \"Lineup Pending\" status, his ability to capitalize on the +5% wind factor and the projected order advantage significantly buffers his base score. **Cal Raleigh** remains an essential pivot, providing the highest daily efficiency at 60.37; while facing a tougher arm in Baz, the +8% boost from hitting second in the order combined with his recent power surge makes him our most reliable anchor. Conversely, **Bryson Stott** (42.81) and **Taylor Ward** (43.53) represent our most marginal starts. Both are facing difficult arms with sub-3.50 xERAs, and while the wind helps mitigate some of the platoon disadvantages, their scores are hovering precariously above our floor.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved balancing the surging potential of **Lawrence Butler** (58.97) against the rigidity of our existing outfield configuration. **Lawrence Butler** actually projected higher than both **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Drew Gilbert**, buoyed by a +10% park factor; however, the lack of an opposing starter data point for his matchup introduced enough variance to keep him in the utility role rather than bumping a clearer platoon advantage. We are also closely monitoring the lineup status for **Masyn Winn**, whose score of 52.03 is heavily dependent on maintaining his position in the lower third of the order. While we are currently carrying **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Yainer Diaz**, and **Tyler Freeman** on the bench due to injuries or off-days, our primary risk for today remains the high percentage of \"Lineup Pending\" designations across the board. Should these official lineups shift away from our projections\u2014specifically moving **Matt Chapman** or **Luis Arraez** down in the order\u2014we will need to re-evaluate the efficiency scores immediately to preserve our season game caps.",
